  "id": "obsessive-compulsive-disorder",
  "term": "Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder",
  "definition": "Obsessive-compulsive disorder is an anxiety disorder marked by recurring, persistent obsessions or compulsions. Obsessions are intrusive ideas, thoughts, or images experienced as senseless or repugnant, while compulsions are repeated, seemingly purposeful behaviors that the person generally recognizes as senseless and not pleasurable, even though they may bring relief from tension.",
